486
00:21:58,560 --> 00:22:00,360
Some kings don't have portraits.

487
00:22:00,720 --> 00:22:02,030
Some have been burned.

488
00:22:02,030 --> 00:22:03,530
Oh, you're right.

489
00:22:03,530 --> 00:22:05,300
Yes, they all burned up during the Imjin War.

490
00:22:05,530 --> 00:22:06,930
So some kings don't have portraits.

491
00:22:06,930 --> 00:22:08,400
(Some royal portraits were lost during wars or fires.)

492
00:22:08,930 --> 00:22:10,430
(In Korea, only the portraits of six kings,)

493
00:22:10,430 --> 00:22:11,770
(King Taejo, King Yeongjo, King Cheoljong, King Ikjong,)

494
00:22:11,770 --> 00:22:13,040
(King Gojong, and King Sunjong remain.)

495
00:22:13,470 --> 00:22:15,540
(There were many royal portraits...)

496
00:22:15,540 --> 00:22:17,740
(that were severely damaged in fires.)

497
00:22:17,740 --> 00:22:19,480
Now that you say that, it's all damaged,

498
00:22:19,480 --> 00:22:22,080
- You're right.
- around the dragon.

499
00:22:22,950 --> 00:22:27,580
(Traces of a tumultuous history can be found around the palace.)

500
00:22:33,620 --> 00:22:35,860
(They get lost in their thoughts as they learn about Huế Palace.)

501
00:22:35,860 --> 00:22:37,890
Oh, it's surprising how similar it is.

502
00:22:42,870 --> 00:22:44,430
We have no architecture from the Kingdoms Period...

503
00:22:44,430 --> 00:22:45,540
because they were all burned up.

504
00:22:45,870 --> 00:22:48,810
Like Baekje. Only the sites are left.

505
00:22:50,170 --> 00:22:51,540
(Leaving the sadness behind,)

506
00:22:51,540 --> 00:22:53,140
(they head over to see another face of Huế Palace.)

507
00:22:54,080 --> 00:22:55,510
This palace is so cool.

508
00:22:56,780 --> 00:22:58,320
(Thế Tổ Miếu, the second course)

509
00:22:58,320 --> 00:22:59,820
(Dien Tho Residence)

510
00:22:59,820 --> 00:23:02,550
The next place is Dien Tho Residence.

511
00:23:02,550 --> 00:23:03,620
Dien Tho Residence.

512
00:23:06,290 --> 00:23:08,460
Even after such a long time...

513
00:23:09,830 --> 00:23:12,360
