- You're a beer enthusiast.
- So this is a great experience.

789
00:34:50,030 --> 00:34:51,530
(Local is best.)

790
00:34:54,960 --> 00:34:56,070
Nice.

791
00:34:58,770 --> 00:35:00,970
It's a bit light and refreshing.

792
00:35:01,340 --> 00:35:02,840
It has its own character.

793
00:35:02,840 --> 00:35:03,940
It's sour.

794
00:35:06,240 --> 00:35:07,380
This is nice.

795
00:35:08,610 --> 00:35:09,980
Water fern cake.

796
00:35:10,450 --> 00:35:11,880
I really love water fern cake.

797
00:35:12,580 --> 00:35:15,520
I really love it. Water fern cake.

798
00:35:20,190 --> 00:35:23,490
(Bánh bèo, Huế's beloved local specialty dish)

799
00:35:24,060 --> 00:35:29,570
(Crispy toppings piled on top of chewy rice dough)

800
00:35:30,100 --> 00:35:35,340
(Bánh bèo, carefully steamed chewy rice cake)

801
00:35:35,570 --> 00:35:38,110
We know how to eat this now.

802
00:35:38,140 --> 00:35:40,180
(Fish sauce)

803
00:35:40,410 --> 00:35:41,740
I love it.

804
00:35:42,080 --> 00:35:43,380
Why is this so good?

805
00:35:46,850 --> 00:35:48,250
I'm having this for two consecutive meals.

806
00:35:48,250 --> 00:35:49,690
(Eating)

807
00:35:53,290 --> 00:35:55,220
This is good.

808
00:35:55,220 --> 00:35:56,790
Why don't they sell this in Korea?

809
00:35:57,930 --> 00:36:00,360
This is like a very high-end drinking snack.

810
00:36:01,800 --> 00:36:02,900
Why is this so good?

811
00:36:08,170 --> 00:36:09,370
It's good, isn't it?

812
00:36:09,970 --> 00:36:11,240
It isn't anything special, though.

813
00:36:27,890 --> 00:36:29,360
This is the best appetizer.

814
00:36:30,990 --> 00:36:33,600
(Empty plates are stacking up.)

815
00:36:35,200 --> 00:36:36,670
We're already leaving tomorrow.

816
00:36:37,000 --> 00:36:39,740
One day is long, but it's not enough when it goes by.

817
00:36:40,100 --> 00:36:41,400
It's already tomorrow.

818
00:36:41,670 --> 00:36:42,910
We took the train today.

819
00:36:42,910 --> 00:36:45,010
We took it today, right? What time is it now?

820
00:36:45,010 --> 00:36:46,140
(Day Three of This is Hyunmoo Road)

821
00:36:46,140 --> 00:36:47,340
It's not even 8pm.

822
00:36:50,210 --> 00:36:53,420
This is the perk of getting up at 5:30am.

823
00:36:53,420 --> 00:36:55,250
That's right. Your day is long.

824
00:36:55,790 --> 00:36:57,790
Yes.

825
00:37:01,220 --> 00:37:03,660
You find this a lot in Korea.

826
00:37:03,660 --> 00:37:05,830
- It's a familiar taste.
- It would have a familiar taste.

827
00:37:06,160 --> 00:37:08,830
We're having Vietnamese food known to Koreans for the first time.

828
00:37:09,470 --> 00:37:10,900
We kept eating unfamiliar food.

829
00:37:25,350 --> 00:37:26,450
It's different.

830
00:37:28,580 --> 00:37:29,690
The filling is different.

831
00:37:29,690 --> 00:37:30,750
What's inside?

832
00:37:31,250 --> 00:37:32,390
Beef.

833
00:37:32,390 --> 00:37:34,660
(Beef is packed generously inside fried spring roll.)

834
00:37:38,860 --> 00:37:40,430
- It's good.
- It tastes different,

835
00:37:40,730 --> 00:37:43,800
- but it's a familiar texture.
- Right.

836
00:37:43,800 --> 00:37:45,070
It's a familiar texture.

837
00:37:49,340 --> 00:37:55,210
(Vietnamese dishes look familiar.)

838
00:37:56,680 --> 00:37:59,880
(But the more you eat, the more you taste the rich local flavours.)

839
00:38:07,020 --> 00:38:08,820
Compared to Thai food,

840
00:38:10,260 --> 00:38:12,700
Vietnamese food feels more similar to Korean food.

841
00:38:14,030 --> 00:38:17,670
Out of all the dishes I had on this trip to Vietnam,

842
00:38:18,470 --> 00:38:21,000
this is the only dish I'd tried before. The rest were new.

843
00:38:21,700 --> 00:38:24,110
- What about you?
- Me too.

844
00:38:24,110 --> 00:38:25,810
How were they all so new?

845
00:38:26,010 --> 00:38:28,840
I've never seen anything like this.

846
00:38:28,840 --> 00:38:30,310
I've never seen it before.

847
00:38:32,150 --> 00:38:33,680
You really like this.

848
00:38:34,520 --> 00:38:36,420
(He responds with his thumb.)

849
00:38:36,950 --> 00:38:40,860
Out of all the dishes you tried in Vietnam...

850
00:38:41,520 --> 00:38:44,260
including desserts, which one ranks first?

851
00:38:44,590 --> 00:38:46,030
From the dishes you tried on this trip.

852
00:38:48,530 --> 00:38:53,040
(Out of all the dishes, which one is Hyun Moo's No. 1 pick?)

853
00:38:53,740 --> 00:38:54,870
What did we have?

854
00:38:55,600 --> 00:38:58,040
(They tried so many dishes that his memory became fuzzy.)

855
00:38:58,040 --> 00:38:59,610
The dish I remember right now...

856
00:39:00,210 --> 00:39:02,040
is the one we found at the market...

857
00:39:02,040 --> 00:39:04,250
and just sat down to eat.

858
00:39:04,250 --> 00:39:06,280
- We had avocado ice cream later.
- Yes.

859
00:39:06,280 --> 00:39:07,820
The combination of those two.

860
00:39:08,480 --> 00:39:11,120
The mini rice pancake and avocado ice cream.

861
00:39:11,120 --> 00:39:12,960
That combination was amazing.

862
00:39:15,620 --> 00:39:17,290
For me, it was baby clam rice.

863
00:39:17,290 --> 00:39:18,730
That was also good.

864
00:39:18,730 --> 00:39:19,930
It was good.

865
00:39:19,930 --> 00:39:22,260
It tasted better than it looked.

866
00:39:24,030 --> 00:39:28,670
(Water fern cake also became his new favourite.)

867
00:39:30,040 --> 00:39:31,340
Why is this so good?

868
00:39:32,580 --> 00:39:33,780
I finished it.

869
00:39:34,480 --> 00:39:36,480
The main dish isn't coming. I want to have the main dish.

870
00:39:37,110 --> 00:39:39,050
These are all familiar tastes.

871
00:39:39,050 --> 00:39:40,120
That's right.

872
00:39:59,300 --> 00:40:02,870
(Stir-fried noodles, a classic Vietnamese fried noodle dish)

873
00:40:04,040 --> 00:40:05,240
Our food's here.

874
00:40:08,010 --> 00:40:09,710
(Vietnamese-style fried noodles with vegetables, meat, and seafood)

875
00:40:09,710 --> 00:40:11,310
Goodness, this...

876
00:40:11,680 --> 00:40:12,950
It's stir-fried noodles.

877
00:40:13,750 --> 00:40:15,220
The colour is interesting.

878
00:40:16,190 --> 00:40:17,650
I wonder what it tastes like.

879
00:40:19,050 --> 00:40:21,820
We're supposed to dip it in this soy sauce, right?

880
00:40:22,490 --> 00:40:24,260
- Right.
- Dip it and eat.

881
00:40:28,130 --> 00:40:29,830
(Eating)

882
00:40:30,170 --> 00:40:32,540
I'll dip the shrimp in soy sauce and have it.

883
00:40:36,710 --> 00:40:38,110
Nice.

884
00:40:39,480 --> 00:40:41,340
I like it because the seafood is fresh.

885
00:40:46,280 --> 00:40:48,780
Then this...

886
00:40:55,160 --> 00:40:56,230
(Exclaiming)

887
00:40:57,090 --> 00:40:58,360
It has a clean taste.

888
00:41:00,900 --> 00:41:03,500
It somewhat seems like Japanese food.

889
00:41:05,270 --> 00:41:06,370
Yakisoba.

890
00:41:07,000 --> 00:41:08,870
It's light and clean, isn't it?

891
00:41:09,240 --> 00:41:10,270
It's got a clean taste.

892
00:41:10,440 --> 00:41:12,210
Right. We kept having spicy food.

893
00:41:12,680 --> 00:41:13,840
Okay.

894
00:41:14,540 --> 00:41:16,210
Are you not happy about all the spicy food?

895
00:41:16,210 --> 00:41:17,450
I'm going to have this spicy.

896
00:41:18,280 --> 00:41:20,120
I can just have plain rice with this.

897
00:41:32,560 --> 00:41:34,530
(His nostrils flare.)

898
00:41:35,330 --> 00:41:36,770
Koreans need to add this in the food.

899
00:41:36,770 --> 00:41:38,530
- Is it better with that?
- Yes.

900
00:41:38,730 --> 00:41:39,740
Should I try it?

901
00:41:40,040 --> 00:41:41,270
It's tasty.

902
00:41:41,270 --> 00:41:42,440
It's really tasty.

903
00:41:45,370 --> 00:41:46,580
You have to put a lot.

904
00:41:46,580 --> 00:41:48,040
(At his age, he wants to like whatever his big brother likes.)

905
00:41:48,040 --> 00:41:50,450
(Are Korean people usually like that?)

906
00:41:50,780 --> 00:41:52,380
(Large chilli flake)

907
00:41:56,620 --> 00:41:57,620
(Satisfied nostrils)

908
00:41:57,620 --> 00:41:59,020
- Right?
- Yes.

909
00:42:01,490 --> 00:42:03,590
It's better with this. I like it spicy.

910
00:42:04,130 --> 00:42:05,790
He likes spicy food.

911
00:42:06,630 --> 00:42:08,360
- We're like twins.
- We're like twins.

912
00:42:08,830 --> 00:42:10,170
It feels very weird.

913
00:42:11,230 --> 00:42:13,170
I like the dishes. They are right up my alley.

914
00:42:13,170 --> 00:42:14,340
That's right.

915
00:42:14,900 --> 00:42:16,970
We also eat about the same amount.

916
00:42:17,870 --> 00:42:19,480
You don't eat like crazy, either.

917
00:42:22,910 --> 00:42:24,580
(Joon's exclamation of satisfaction)

918
00:42:26,120 --> 00:42:27,820
Okay, let's go.

919
00:42:33,060 --> 00:42:35,020
- It's sold out.
- It's sold out.

920
00:42:35,020 --> 00:42:37,360
- Nice.
- Perfect timing.

921
00:42:37,560 --> 00:42:39,730
I guess the dishes got sold out...

922
00:42:39,960 --> 00:42:41,730
because we ordered a lot.

923
00:42:42,730 --> 00:42:43,870
Thank you.

924
00:42:45,670 --> 00:42:51,440
(A delicious and eventful third night in Vietnam)

925
00:43:00,250 --> 00:43:01,780
(Vietnam's morning...)

926
00:43:01,780 --> 00:43:04,550
(filled with the footsteps of early risers)

927
00:43:05,550 --> 00:43:07,460
(The sounds of busy motorbikes...)

928
00:43:07,460 --> 00:43:10,290
(blend with the morning birdsong.)

929
00:43:12,190 --> 00:43:13,660
Nice.

930
00:43:13,800 --> 00:43:16,670
We always start our mornings early.

931
00:43:16,670 --> 00:43:19,400
I normally start my days early when I'm travelling.

932
00:43:19,400 --> 00:43:21,170
- Really?
- I go to bed early.

933
00:43:21,170 --> 00:43:23,470
Mornings are more fun wherever you go.

934
00:43:23,470 --> 00:43:25,840
I tend to sleep in.

935
00:43:25,840 --> 00:43:26,940
Until around 9am.

936
00:43:27,240 --> 00:43:29,080
If we go out in the morning,

937
00:43:29,080 --> 00:43:31,680
we can really see the country,

938
00:43:31,680 --> 00:43:33,550
which fits the concept of our show.

939
00:43:34,150 --> 00:43:38,120
We can see how the locals live as we walk around in the morning.

940
00:43:38,150 --> 00:43:39,250
Right.

941
00:43:39,390 --> 00:43:42,590
I wonder when the people here usually get up.

942
00:43:42,590 --> 00:43:44,230
- I wonder.
- It seems like...

943
00:43:44,230 --> 00:43:46,860
- they get up around 5 to 5:30am.
- I think they get up early.

944
00:43:47,700 --> 00:43:50,570
(People have already started their day.)

945
00:43:50,700 --> 00:43:53,300
- They're all eating.
- It's already full.

946
00:43:53,740 --> 00:43:54,840
It's full.

947
00:43:55,400 --> 00:43:56,870
I just saw something shocking.

948
00:43:57,570 --> 00:43:59,040
What?

949
00:43:59,940 --> 00:44:01,310
- That's Suzy.
- Are you serious?

950
00:44:01,580 --> 00:44:03,680
(They see a familiar face in a foreign land.)

951
00:44:04,150 --> 00:44:05,180
Oh, it is!

952
00:44:05,780 --> 00:44:06,880
It is her.

953
00:44:07,350 --> 00:44:09,420
- It's really her.
- Right?

954
00:44:09,420 --> 00:44:11,120
It blends in so well, though.

955
00:44:11,120 --> 00:44:13,660
Wasn't MBLAQ active around the time miss A was?

956
00:44:13,660 --> 00:44:15,460
- Yes, it was the same period.
- Right?

957
00:44:15,690 --> 00:44:18,560
- That's amazing.
- Suzy was in Huế.

958
00:44:18,560 --> 00:44:19,960
(Hi.)

959
00:44:20,300 --> 00:44:22,560
Where are we going, by the way?

960
00:44:23,170 --> 00:44:26,570
Let's find a square where people are.

961
00:44:28,300 --> 00:44:30,310
It's so lively here.

962
00:44:30,440 --> 00:44:32,410
They go around you when you cross the street.

963
00:44:33,640 --> 00:44:34,680
Right?

964
00:44:34,680 --> 00:44:36,380
(He can easily cross the street now that it's been 4 days.)

965
00:44:39,310 --> 00:44:41,220
- It's Janggi.
- They're playing Janggi.

966
00:44:43,090 --> 00:44:47,160
(The locals are playing a type of chess.)

967
00:44:47,390 --> 00:44:48,660
Are you good at Janggi?

968
00:44:48,720 --> 00:44:50,290
- I'm pretty good, - Okay.

969
00:44:50,560 --> 00:44:52,060
but it looks a bit different from ours.

970
00:44:54,030 --> 00:44:56,530
(A popular hobby in Vietnam, Janggi)

971
00:44:58,170 --> 00:45:02,340
(The Janggi rules in Vietnam are a little different from Korean's.)

972
00:45:08,740 --> 00:45:10,810
He just moved his pawn laterally.

973
00:45:10,810 --> 00:45:12,080
(Hyun Moo studies the Vietnamese Janggi.)

974
00:45:12,080 --> 00:45:14,350
So, it moves like a rook when it's not attacking.

975
00:45:14,450 --> 00:45:16,220
(He knows nothing about Janggi.)

976
00:45:16,320 --> 00:45:17,320
(Making eye contact)

977
00:45:17,320 --> 00:45:18,320
(Standing up)

978
00:45:18,720 --> 00:45:20,020
(Would you like to sit?)

979
00:45:20,020 --> 00:45:21,490
(People here are so generous.)

980
00:45:22,320 --> 00:45:24,260
We can just...

981
00:45:25,260 --> 00:45:26,400
Oh, we move it down?

982
00:45:26,400 --> 00:45:27,530
(A sudden Janggi match)

983
00:45:27,530 --> 00:45:28,630
Oh, like this?

984
00:45:29,430 --> 00:45:31,530
Korea versus Vietnam. The match starts now.

985
00:45:31,530 --> 00:45:33,640
(Janggi match, Korea versus Vietnam)

986
00:45:34,740 --> 00:45:36,970
(An expert morning player from Vietnam)

987
00:45:37,510 --> 00:45:39,810
(And Hyun Moo goes against him, representing Korea.)

988
00:45:39,810 --> 00:45:42,040
(Looking solemn)

989
00:45:44,610 --> 00:45:45,980
(He discreetly moves the first piece.)

990
00:45:45,980 --> 00:45:47,250
(Moving)

991
00:45:47,520 --> 00:45:49,590
They're really fast with it.

992
00:45:49,590 --> 00:45:50,890
He instantly moved it.

993
00:45:51,290 --> 00:45:52,690
I can stop you if you play that way.

994
00:45:53,160 --> 00:45:54,860
(Laughing)

995
00:45:55,290 --> 00:45:58,090
At least you didn't lose any pieces yet.

996
00:45:58,660 --> 00:45:59,960
- Oh, no.
- It's fine.

997
00:45:59,960 --> 00:46:01,160
- No!
- I can take one too.

998
00:46:01,630 --> 00:46:03,030
Yes, it's still looking okay.

999
00:46:04,500 --> 00:46:07,200
(The local looks relaxed compared to Hyun Moo who's serious.)

1000
00:46:07,200 --> 00:46:08,200
(Hyun Moo is flustered.)

1001
00:46:08,340 --> 00:46:09,400
What?

1002
00:46:10,070 --> 00:46:11,110
What?

1003
00:46:12,510 --> 00:46:14,280
- It's over?
- You lost.

1004
00:46:14,280 --> 00:46:16,080
- Okay.
- It's over? Really?

1005
00:46:17,080 --> 00:46:19,110
Okay. Thank you.

1006
00:46:19,110 --> 00:46:21,480
(He lost in 3 minutes, but it was a fun match.)

1007
00:46:23,350 --> 00:46:25,450
- Thank you!
- That was fast.

1008
00:46:25,450 --> 00:46:27,190
(Have fun in Vietnam.)

1009
00:46:27,190 --> 00:46:28,420
Maybe you lost because the rules were different.

1010
00:46:28,420 --> 00:46:29,930
Obviously.

1011
00:46:29,930 --> 00:46:31,930
If we had played by Korean rules, I would have easily beaten him.

1012
00:46:31,930 --> 00:46:33,560
(Laughing)

1013
00:46:37,230 --> 00:46:39,370
This place is...

1014
00:46:40,100 --> 00:46:41,800
- What?
- It's...

1015
00:46:42,470 --> 00:46:44,540
- They're...
- They're even neatly dressed.

1016
00:46:44,540 --> 00:46:45,770
They're so diligent.

1017
00:46:46,540 --> 00:46:48,210
Are they filming a workout video?

1018
00:46:48,380 --> 00:46:50,280
- They're dancing. It's aerobics.
- Goodness.

1019
00:46:50,280 --> 00:46:51,650
(Aerobics)

1020
00:46:51,650 --> 00:46:53,320
It's so healthy.

1021
00:46:53,980 --> 00:46:57,420
(There's something you can easily see in the morning.)

1022
00:46:57,850 --> 00:47:01,060
(Locals who exercise, mostly aerobics and yoga)

1023
00:47:01,060 --> 00:47:03,360
(Dawn is the best time as it's the coolest time of the day.)

1024
00:47:04,460 --> 00:47:06,260
(Men and women of all ages enjoy...)

1025
00:47:06,260 --> 00:47:08,030
(a good morning workout.)

1026
00:47:09,160 --> 00:47:11,100
It's aerobics or Zumba.

1027
00:47:11,470 --> 00:47:12,970
- Yes, Zumba.
- Yes.

1028
00:47:20,140 --> 00:47:22,680
(Joon's hips start moving.)

1029
00:47:23,580 --> 00:47:25,250
(Join us.)

1030
00:47:25,250 --> 00:47:26,280
We must.

1031
00:47:26,280 --> 00:47:27,380
(We have to join them.)

1032
00:47:31,150 --> 00:47:33,320
(The two men enter the stage while dancing.)

1033
00:47:33,320 --> 00:47:35,760
They're dancing in the morning.

1034
00:47:36,090 --> 00:47:37,330
Even yesterday...

1035
00:47:38,660 --> 00:47:40,100
Should we squeeze in?

1036
00:47:40,100 --> 00:47:41,760
(He looks for spots to go into.)

1037
00:47:42,400 --> 00:47:43,400
(Clapping)

1038
00:47:44,400 --> 00:47:45,400
(Clapping)

1039
00:47:45,400 --> 00:47:46,940
(Awkward)

1040
00:47:47,270 --> 00:47:49,610
(Joon has already gotten the hang of it.)

1041
00:47:53,240 --> 00:47:55,610
(The two men are now one with the local moms.)

1042
00:48:02,080 --> 00:48:03,550
(Peeking)

1043
00:48:04,790 --> 00:48:08,120
(Same-side hands and feet)

1044
00:48:08,660 --> 00:48:11,360
(Hyun Moo is more serious than ever.)

1045
00:48:12,160 --> 00:48:14,630
(Ah-ha)

1046
00:48:14,630 --> 00:48:15,760
(Ting, ting, ting, ting, tang, tang, tang, tang)

1047
00:48:15,760 --> 00:48:18,500
(They don't even stand out anymore.)

1048
00:48:18,500 --> 00:48:20,370
(Don't be sad)

1049
00:48:20,370 --> 00:48:22,370
(Just like the leaves falling outside the front yard)

1050
00:48:22,370 --> 00:48:24,410
(My heart flutters at the lively laughter)

1051
00:48:24,410 --> 00:48:26,410
(Echoing through the wind-swayed trees)

1052
