It's like the exercise I do every morning.

1567
01:10:48,520 --> 01:10:49,820
(I work out every morning. This is easy.)

1568
01:10:52,150 --> 01:10:53,150
Why did I bother to shower?

1569
01:10:53,150 --> 01:10:55,020
If we go all the way there, I don't think we can make it back.

1570
01:10:55,720 --> 01:10:57,990
There's no way we'll make it back. I'm dying.

1571
01:10:58,690 --> 01:10:59,690
(I'm dying!)

1572
01:11:00,230 --> 01:11:01,400
Is their boat better?

1573
01:11:01,860 --> 01:11:03,730
I think their boat is better. Does it have a motor?

1574
01:11:04,670 --> 01:11:05,900
- Do we turn around here?
- Turn around!

1575
01:11:07,230 --> 01:11:08,970
- Turn around!
- Turn around!

1576
01:11:09,440 --> 01:11:11,510
Turn around!

1577
01:11:12,370 --> 01:11:14,740
We're being so shameless here.

1578
01:11:18,010 --> 01:11:21,680
(Two cheaters cut the inside corner to take the lead.)

1579
01:11:22,950 --> 01:11:25,220
No!

1580
01:11:25,220 --> 01:11:27,390
(Not fair!)

1581
01:11:28,690 --> 01:11:30,220
(A sneaky shortcut takes the lead.)

1582
01:11:30,220 --> 01:11:31,360
Turn around!

1583
01:11:34,090 --> 01:11:37,330
Most Koreans don't do this.

1584
01:11:38,870 --> 01:11:40,930
- I'm so sorry.
- No!

1585
01:11:41,970 --> 01:11:44,410
What is this?

1586
01:11:45,710 --> 01:11:46,770
I'm so sorry.

1587
01:11:46,770 --> 01:11:48,880
Aren't we being ugly Koreans here?

1588
01:11:48,880 --> 01:11:49,940
Okay.

1589
01:11:51,750 --> 01:11:52,910
(So much for cheating)

1590
01:11:52,910 --> 01:11:54,150
(Team Vietnam quickly catches up.)

1591
01:11:54,380 --> 01:11:55,620
Goodness.

1592
01:11:55,980 --> 01:11:57,580
They are relaxed.

1593
01:11:57,580 --> 01:11:59,550
Hurry and pedal.

1594
01:11:59,790 --> 01:12:00,990
- They're beating us.
- What? This is crazy.

1595
01:12:00,990 --> 01:12:02,360
- Hurry!
- Should we go?

1596
01:12:02,360 --> 01:12:03,390
- Let's hurry.
- Go?

1597
01:12:03,560 --> 01:12:04,590
Go!

1598
01:12:04,590 --> 01:12:06,030
(Here we come!)

1599
01:12:06,030 --> 01:12:07,090
This is so tiring.

1600
01:12:07,530 --> 01:12:08,800
Bye!

1601
01:12:10,730 --> 01:12:12,900
(The gap just keeps growing.)

1602
01:12:13,500 --> 01:12:14,700
(We can't lose like this!)

1603
01:12:14,700 --> 01:12:15,870
Die!

1604
01:12:15,870 --> 01:12:17,710
- Pedal!
- Gosh!

1605
01:12:18,410 --> 01:12:20,570
- Joon, pedal!
- Gosh!

1606
01:12:22,610 --> 01:12:23,680
Let's go!

1607
01:12:27,150 --> 01:12:29,720
They are so happy.

1608
01:12:29,720 --> 01:12:31,690
- Hyun Moo.
- You're a gym buff!

1609
01:12:32,720 --> 01:12:34,590
(But there's a flaw in Joon's workout routine.)

1610
01:12:34,960 --> 01:12:37,190
(All strength, no cardio)

1611
01:12:38,530 --> 01:12:39,830
This is so embarrassing.

1612
01:12:39,830 --> 01:12:41,300
Who rides the swan boat like this?

1613
01:12:42,800 --> 01:12:43,960
Why aren't you pedalling?

1614
01:12:43,960 --> 01:12:46,300
I am pedalling! Look at me.

1615
01:12:46,730 --> 01:12:48,270
We should be enjoying the ride like them.

1616
01:12:48,770 --> 01:12:50,940
- What are we doing?
- Wait. We will bump into it.

1617
01:12:50,940 --> 01:12:51,970
We won't.

1618
01:12:52,170 --> 01:12:53,710
The weather is very nice.

1619
01:12:56,980 --> 01:12:58,310
I'm afraid we will bump into them.

1620
01:12:59,880 --> 01:13:01,420
It's not over yet!

1621
01:13:01,580 --> 01:13:03,250
- I think it is.
- No.

1622
01:13:03,580 --> 01:13:05,820
Pedal! Pedal, Joon!

1623
01:13:05,820 --> 01:13:07,490
(The finish line is getting closer.)

1624
01:13:09,060 --> 01:13:11,430
Let's go!

1625
01:13:12,060 --> 01:13:15,700
(Their co-workers cheer them on during their company outing.)

1626
01:13:17,000 --> 01:13:18,930
(Team Vietnam gets a boost from the cheers.)

1627
01:13:20,930 --> 01:13:22,870
I said, pedal! Last spurt!

1628
01:13:22,870 --> 01:13:24,670
(One last chance to take the lead)

1629
01:13:24,670 --> 01:13:25,670
Gosh.

1630
01:13:26,570 --> 01:13:27,710
Why isn't this moving forward?

1631
01:13:27,840 --> 01:13:29,610
It's barely moving. The pedals are so stiff.

1632
01:13:30,040 --> 01:13:31,350
Welcome to Vietnam!

1633
01:13:35,580 --> 01:13:37,480
No way.

1634
01:13:37,480 --> 01:13:40,490
(As expected, Team Vietnam crosses the finish line first.)

1635
01:13:40,490 --> 01:13:42,120
Last spurt!

1636
01:13:42,120 --> 01:13:44,120
(Puttering along...)

1637
01:13:44,560 --> 01:13:45,890
- Touched it!
- Touched it!

1638
01:13:45,890 --> 01:13:47,860
(The Vietnam versus Korea swan boat race is over.)

1639
01:13:48,130 --> 01:13:49,630
Okay.

1640
01:13:49,630 --> 01:13:51,500
- Congratulations!
- Good job.

1641
01:13:52,030 --> 01:13:53,200
This is unbelievable.

1642
01:13:53,730 --> 01:13:56,070
They're pros. Are they rowers?

1643
01:13:56,340 --> 01:13:57,700
They are professionals.

1644
01:13:58,640 --> 01:14:01,140
They're not even out of breath.

1645
01:14:01,510 --> 01:14:03,410
- Their boat must have a motor.
- I think their boat...

1646
01:14:03,410 --> 01:14:04,610
(Neither can accept defeat.)

1647
01:14:04,610 --> 01:14:05,710
is different.

1648
01:14:06,680 --> 01:14:07,750
Unbelievable.

1649
01:14:08,350 --> 01:14:09,750
Let's go.

1650
01:14:10,850 --> 01:14:12,820
How often do you guys practice?

1651
01:14:13,190 --> 01:14:15,160
- This?
- Yes.

1652
01:14:15,160 --> 01:14:17,420
We have been doing it since we were five years old.

1653
01:14:17,620 --> 01:14:18,960
Since you were five years old?

1654
01:14:19,160 --> 01:14:20,760
They're pros! Athlete.

1655
01:14:21,360 --> 01:14:22,600
- You guys are...
- If they've been doing it...

1656
01:14:22,800 --> 01:14:24,130
athletes. Like athletes.

1657
01:14:24,300 --> 01:14:26,430
But you did a really good job too.

1658
01:14:26,430 --> 01:14:27,470
No, no good job.

1659
01:14:27,470 --> 01:14:28,500
(No good job)

1660
01:14:28,600 --> 01:14:29,870
We did a very bad job.

1661
01:14:31,370 --> 01:14:32,570
I travel...

1662
01:14:33,170 --> 01:14:34,740
all over the world.

1663
01:14:34,740 --> 01:14:37,540
This country is the first country...

1664
01:14:37,950 --> 01:14:39,450
I started.

1665
01:14:39,610 --> 01:14:40,910
Vietnam!

1666
01:14:40,910 --> 01:14:42,580
Vietnam!

1667
01:14:42,650 --> 01:14:44,450
I hope you will love Vietnam.

1668
01:14:44,450 --> 01:14:46,750
- I love it.
- Thank you so much.

1669
01:14:46,750 --> 01:14:48,560
- You are the winners!
- Winners!

1670
01:14:48,560 --> 01:14:51,830
(Ride a swan boat or skip it: regrets either way)

1671
01:14:53,830 --> 01:14:55,300
- Okay.
- Okay.

1672
01:14:55,300 --> 01:14:57,060
- Okay!
- Have a nice day.

1673
01:14:57,060 --> 01:14:58,130
- Thank you.
- Have a nice day.

1674
01:14:58,130 --> 01:14:59,370
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1675
01:14:59,370 --> 01:15:01,300
(Priceless, happy memories made with the locals)

1676
01:15:01,400 --> 01:15:02,570
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1677
01:15:04,200 --> 01:15:05,410
It was a good match.

1678
01:15:06,110 --> 01:15:07,980
We didn't get to enjoy the boat ride at all.

1679
01:15:08,780 --> 01:15:09,840
I'm exhausted.

1680
01:15:12,210 --> 01:15:14,410
Let's just enjoy the sunset.

1681
01:15:14,410 --> 01:15:15,420
It's...

1682
01:15:15,980 --> 01:15:17,580
about 6:10pm now,

1683
01:15:17,580 --> 01:15:19,220
so the sun should set around 6:30pm.

1684
01:15:19,220 --> 01:15:21,890
We should be able to watch it sitting somewhere like that.

1685
01:15:22,820 --> 01:15:24,160
(The perfect time to sit back and enjoy the sunset)

1686
01:15:24,160 --> 01:15:26,560
This reminds me of Nodeul Island.

1687
01:15:28,030 --> 01:15:29,360
I think it's time we actually enjoyed ourselves.

1688
01:15:29,360 --> 01:15:32,770
(This time, just peace. No more wearing themselves out.)

1689
01:15:33,330 --> 01:15:35,440
But seriously, the view over there is incredible.

1690
01:15:35,440 --> 01:15:36,640
Those clouds, and this whole stretch...

1691
01:15:36,640 --> 01:15:37,800
I need to take a photo too.

1692
01:15:38,140 --> 01:15:39,340
It's one big panorama.

1693
01:15:39,340 --> 01:15:41,140
(Sitting by the river, they take in the sunset.)

1694
01:15:41,140 --> 01:15:42,440
What a view.

1695
01:15:43,710 --> 01:15:46,180
It does feel a little different from the Han River.

1696
01:15:46,280 --> 01:15:47,310
Completely different.

1697
01:15:48,250 --> 01:15:50,250
This is a Huế sunset.

1698
01:15:53,590 --> 01:15:55,420
Think of it as the Han River with even more natural scenery.

1699
01:16:05,300 --> 01:16:06,330
It's beautiful.

1700
01:16:06,330 --> 01:16:07,970
(As the sunset settles, the scene grows even more peaceful.)

1701
01:16:07,970 --> 01:16:08,970
Gosh.

1702
01:16:09,240 --> 01:16:10,900
We started in Da Nang...

1703
01:16:11,510 --> 01:16:12,940
and made our way to Huế.

1704
01:16:13,270 --> 01:16:15,210
We tried all that Huế food this morning, too.

1705
01:16:15,210 --> 01:16:16,740
We had bún bò Huế.

1706
01:16:17,840 --> 01:16:20,950
(Bún bò Huế: one of Vietnam's top three rice noodle soups)

1707
01:16:21,450 --> 01:16:24,750
(Bánh bèo: a Huế specialty with a distinctive flavour)

1708
01:16:24,750 --> 01:16:26,490
And the freshwater clam soup.

1709
01:16:26,590 --> 01:16:28,090
- Right. That was good.
- That was so good.

1710
01:16:28,090 --> 01:16:29,160
(Freshwater clams that hit the spot)

1711
01:16:29,160 --> 01:16:30,360
We had that, too.

1712
01:16:31,930 --> 01:16:34,460
And in Da Nang, we went way off the tourist trail.

1713
01:16:35,130 --> 01:16:37,160
(Everyone here is Vietnamese.)

1714
01:16:37,760 --> 01:16:41,640
(Out of all these people, there isn't a single Korean.)

1715
01:16:41,770 --> 01:16:44,240
We just threw ourselves into the crowd.

1716
01:16:44,240 --> 01:16:45,610
To see how people live.

1717
01:16:46,070 --> 01:16:47,510
The trip has been fun, but what really moved me was...

1718
01:16:47,510 --> 01:16:49,140
Their eyes look so kind.

1719
01:16:49,140 --> 01:16:52,850
(Kindness in their eyes hit them before a word was spoken.)

1720
01:16:52,980 --> 01:16:55,650
They're so easygoing and so kind.

1721
01:16:55,980 --> 01:16:57,120
That's what really moved me.

1722
01:16:57,120 --> 01:16:59,890
(The down-to-earth, friendly people of Vietnam)

1723
01:17:00,090 --> 01:17:03,960
The fact that we're making our own path...

1724
01:17:05,230 --> 01:17:06,660
That will stay with me for a long time.

1725
01:17:06,790 --> 01:17:09,030
I think it might even change the way I travel from now on.

1726
01:17:09,530 --> 01:17:10,700
Aren't I a good travel buddy?

1727
01:17:10,700 --> 01:17:12,770
- You were the best, honestly.
- Be honest.

1728
01:17:12,770 --> 01:17:14,330
- How would you rate me out of 10?
- It's definitely 10.

1729
01:17:14,330 --> 01:17:16,940
I'd give you more than ten if I could.

1730
01:17:17,140 --> 01:17:18,310
It's been really great.

1731
01:17:18,310 --> 01:17:20,640
Tell me where you want to go next.

1732
01:17:20,810 --> 01:17:23,440
Let's take trips now and then and blow off some stress.

1733
01:17:23,440 --> 01:17:24,480
Yes.

1734
01:17:24,710 --> 01:17:27,180
We've got to end this with a photo.

1735
01:17:27,180 --> 01:17:29,080
Looking at the sunset...

1736
01:17:31,150 --> 01:17:32,350
I mean, with the sunset behind us.

1737
01:17:33,050 --> 01:17:34,390
This looks like a movie.

1738
01:17:36,420 --> 01:17:37,460
That's a great shot.

1739
01:17:53,510 --> 01:17:55,180
(Goodbye, Vietnam)

1740
01:17:55,180 --> 01:17:56,680
(Travel itinerary available on our official social media account)

1741
01:17:56,680 --> 01:17:58,250
(Travel itinerary available on our official social media account)

1742
01:17:58,250 --> 01:18:00,550
(This is Hyunmoo Road Next Destination)

1743
01:18:02,280 --> 01:18:03,950
(This Is Hyunmoo Road's second destination)

1744
01:18:03,950 --> 01:18:06,150
(A small-city tour of Japan: Tokushima)

1745
01:18:06,390 --> 01:18:07,890
(The theme for our second trip)

1746
01:18:07,890 --> 01:18:10,420
(All-in-one)

1747
01:18:10,790 --> 01:18:13,330
(An all-in-one guest on This Is Hyunmoo Road?)

1748
01:18:13,760 --> 01:18:15,830
(Actor and all-around entertainer Kim Nam Gil)

1749
01:18:16,230 --> 01:18:18,100
(Three men, one all-in-one adventure?)

1750
01:18:18,100 --> 01:18:19,100
(Activities)

1751
01:18:19,930 --> 01:18:20,930
(Screaming)

1752
01:18:21,100 --> 01:18:22,100
(I'm scared!)

1753
01:18:22,700 --> 01:18:23,700
It's terrifying.

1754
01:18:23,700 --> 01:18:25,210
(Pants-wetting thrills)

1755
01:18:25,210 --> 01:18:27,540
(Nature that's a work of art)

1756
01:18:27,540 --> 01:18:30,110
(Relaxation: maxed out)

1757
01:18:30,110 --> 01:18:31,580
(Art that commands the space)

1758
01:18:31,850 --> 01:18:32,950
(I got goosebumps.)

1759
01:18:32,950 --> 01:18:36,180
(Food)

1760
01:18:37,220 --> 01:18:38,250
(Love at first bite)

1761
01:18:38,390 --> 01:18:39,450
So soft.

1762
01:18:40,220 --> 01:18:41,220
(The best)

1763
01:18:41,220 --> 01:18:42,390
(How much is this?)

1764
01:18:42,460 --> 01:18:44,620
(1,250 dollars for food)

1765
01:18:44,620 --> 01:18:46,060
(All in on food?)
